blyopia affect educational, health, and social outcomes? Findings from 1958 British birth cohort. BMJ 332:820&#x02013;825. doi:10.1136/bmj.38751.597963.AE <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16520328</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cole</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Beck</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Moke</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The Amblyopia treatment index</article-title><source>J AAPOS</source><year>2001</year><volume>5</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>250</fpage><lpage>254</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1067/mpa.2001.117097</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Cole SR, Beck RW, Moke PS et al (2001) The Amblyopia treatment index. J AAPOS 5(4):250&#x02013;254. doi:10.1067/mpa.2001.117097 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11507585</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Simonsz-T&#x000f3;th</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Visusevaluierung in einer historischen Kohorte von 137 okkludierten Patienten, 30&#x02013;35&#x000a0;Jahre nach Ende der Okklusionsbehandlung (Evaluation of visual acuity in a historic cohort of 137 patients treated for amblyopia by occlusion 30&#x02013;35&#x000a0;years ago)</article-title><source>Klin Monatsbl Augenheilkd</source><year>2007</year><volume>224</volume><fpage>40</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1055/s-2006-927209</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Simonsz-T&#x000f3;th B et al (2007) Visusevaluierung in einer historischen Kohorte von 137 okkludierten Patienten, 30&#x02013;35&#x000a0;Jahre nach Ende der Okklusionsbehandlung (Evaluation of visual acuity in a historic cohort of 137 patients treated for amblyopia by occlusion 30&#x02013;35&#x000a0;years ago). Klin Monatsbl Augenheilkd 224:40&#x02013;46. doi:10.1055/s-2006-927209 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17260318</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ford</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Madow</surname><given-names>WG</given-names></name><name><surname>Ollein</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Rubin</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Anti-inflammatory agents&#x02013;steroids as anti-inflammatory agents</article-title><source>Incomplete data in sample surveys</source><year>1983</year><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>New York Press</publisher-name><fpage>185</fpage><lpage>207</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Ford BL (1983) An overview of hot-deck procedures. In: Madow WG, Ollein I, Rubin DB (Eds) Incomplete data in sample surveys. New York Press, New York, pp 185-207 </citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Armitage</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Berry</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Matthews</surname><given-names>JNS</given-names></name></person-group><source>Statistical methods in medical research</source><year>2001</year><edition>4</edition><publisher-loc>Oxford</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Blackwell Publishing Inc</publisher-name><fpage>456</fpage><lpage>464</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Armitage P, Berry G, Matthews JNS (2001) Statistical methods in medical research, 4th edn. Blackwell Publishing Inc, Oxford, pp 456&#x02013;464 </citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-g